---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — SmartLukuFitness" description="Learn about SmartLukuFitness and our core three pillars: Style, Fitness, and Lifestyle for busy working professionals.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT</p>
      <h1>SmartLukuFitness is a lifestyle platform about intentional living.</h1>
      <p>
        “Luku” is Nairobi Sheng for looking smart, dressing well, or throwing a good outfit. SmartLukuFitness takes that idea further. Being Smart Luku is about making intentional choices in how you present yourself, how you move, and how you organize your everyday working life.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="container pillar-grid about-grid">
      <article class="pillar-card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Dress smart</span>
        <h2>Style</h2>
        <p>Corporate, modest, and smart casual dressing built for real working days in Kenya — plus a transparent journey into learning fashion design from the ground up.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="pillar-card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Move smart</span>
        <h2>Fitness</h2>
        <p>Practical 30-minute workouts, no-equipment home routines, and workday movement breaks designed around busy professional schedules.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="pillar-card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Live smart</span>
        <h2>Lifestyle</h2>
        <p>Practical routines, time management systems, weekly preparation, and personal organization that simplify everyday working life.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="container about-story" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <div class="card" style="padding: 2rem;">
        <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">The Design Journey Story</h2>
        <p>
          Beyond styling, SmartLukuFitness is documenting an ongoing, transparent progression into fashion design. Creator Nancy Wambui is studying garment theory, pattern drafting, fabric behaviour, and sewing-machine construction step by step.
        </p>
        <p>
          The goal is not claiming instant designer status, but documenting a genuine craft journey from understanding clothing to learning how to create it.
        </p>
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/design-journey/`} class="btn btn-secondary" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">Follow the Design Journey →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
